rs-5-2","title":"Lesson XXVIII: The Passive of regō and audiō — Perseus (Continued)","steps":["Learn the passive of regō and audiō in three tenses; note regeris, not regiris","Translate Exercise I and put Exercise II into Latin","Learn the vocabulary and read what the oracle answered Cepheus"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXVIII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/18251/pg18251-images.html#lesson_XXVIII"},{"label":"Special vocabulary for Lesson XXVIII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/18251/pg18251-images.html#sec171vocab"}],"pages":"pp. 72–73","questions":["Translate: mittentur","Write in Latin: it is said","What did the oracle tell Cepheus to give the monster?"],"answers":["They will be sent","Dīcitur","His daughter Andromeda"]},{"id":"latin-for-beginners-5-3","title":"Lesson XXIX: The Passive of -iō Verbs; Infinitive and Imperative","steps":["Learn the passive of capiō in three tenses","Learn the present infinitives, active and passive, and the passive imperative","Learn the vocabulary; translate Exercise I and put Exercise II into Latin"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXIX","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/18251/pg18251-images.html#lesson_XXIX"},{"label":"Special vocabulary for Lesson XXIX","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/18251/pg18251-images.html#sec176vocab"}],"pages":"pp. 73–75","questions":["Give the present passive infinitive of mittō.","Give the present passive infinitive of audiō.","Translate: Mōnstrum est validum, tamen superābitur."],"answers":["Mittī","Audīrī","The monster is strong, yet it will be overcome"]},{"id":"latin-for-beginners-5-4","title":"Lesson XXX: Synopses; the Ablative Denoting From","steps":["Practice synopses (§ 177) of rapiō, mūniō, doceō, and laudō in several persons","Learn the rules for place from which, separation, and the personal agent; compare sagittā with ā Diānā","Learn the vocabulary; translate Exercise I and put Exercise II into Latin"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXX","url"