tō.","Translate: Perseus ad terram dēscendit.","What did Cepheus promise Perseus if he killed the monster?"],"answers":["Mīsī","Perseus came down to the earth","Andromeda as his wife"]},{"id":"latin-for-beginners-5-7","title":"Lesson XXXIII: The Pluperfect and Future Perfect Active; Perfect Infinitive","steps":["Inflect the pluperfect (-eram) and future perfect (-erō) of the five model verbs","Form the perfect active infinitive with -isse","Translate Exercise I and put Exercise II into Latin"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXIII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/18251/pg18251-images.html#lesson_XXXIII"}],"pages":"pp. 84–86","questions":["Translate: discesserāmus","Give the perfect active infinitive of videō.","Write in Latin: they have obeyed"],"answers":["We had departed","Vīdisse","Pāruērunt"]},{"id":"latin-for-beginners-5-8","title":"Lesson XXXIV: Review of the Active Voice — Perseus (Concluded)","steps":["Learn the table of how each active tense is formed (§ 197)","Give quick synopses of five verbs from § 198 and learn the perfects in § 199","Learn the vocabulary and read the end of Perseus and Andromeda, explaining each perfect and imperfect"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXIV","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/18251/pg18251-images.html#lesson_XXXIV"},{"label":"Special vocabulary for Lesson XXXIV","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/18251/pg18251-images.html#sec200vocab"}],"pages":"pp. 86–88","questions":["How is the pluperfect active formed?","Give the perfect of reperiō.","Translate: Perseus mōnstrum interfēcit."],"answers":["Perfect stem + -eram","Repperī","Perseus killed the monster"]},{"id":"latin-for-beginners-5-9","title":"Lesson XXXV: The Passive Perfects; Perfect Passive and Future Active Infinitives","steps":["Learn the fourth principal part and the participial stem","Form the perfect, pluperfect, and future perfect passive with sum, making the participle agree","Translate Exercise I and put Exercise II into Latin"],"