n together","Slate work: copy “How fast the cars go!”","Read the script exercise aloud, then copy it"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXX","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00286"}],"questions":["Why can''t the mill wheel go round?","Who had a fall?"],"answers":["There is ice on the pond","John"],"notes":"Review lesson: no new words. Let your child read it as independently as possible and note any words to revisit. This page has a script (cursive) exercise to read and copy."}]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-u7","title":"Unit 7: Lessons XXXI–XXXV","lessons":[{"id":"mcguffey-primer-7-1","title":"Lesson XXXI: Hard at Work","steps":["New words: work, ax, pile, Ned, think, wood, saw, hard, cut; sound focus: th (think); or sound in work","Let your child read the lesson aloud slowly; help only on words they can''t sound out","Slate work: copy “John has a saw.”","Answer the lesson''s question: can they cut it all in one day?"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXI","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00296"}],"questions":["What tool does John have?","What tool does Ned have?"],"answers":["A saw","An ax"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-7-2","title":"Lesson XXXII: A Walk in May","steps":["New words: noise, air, hear, gone, May, walk, cool, two; sound focus: oi; long a (May)","Read it once aloud for your child, then have them read it to you (or to a sibling or stuffed animal)","Slate work: copy “Two girls have gone out for a walk.”","Take a short walk and listen, like the girls; name what you hear"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00303"}],"questions":["What month is it?","What two sounds do the girls hear?"],"answers":["May","Birds singing and frogs in the pond"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-7-3","title":"Lesson XXXIII: Bess and Her Goats","steps":["New words: pull, cart, goats, Bess, up, ride, hill; sound focus: short u (up); u in pull","Read the lesson aloud together, pointing to each word; then let your child read it alone","Slate work: copy “She likes to ride in her cart.”","Narrate: why do the goats love Bess?"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXIII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00310"}],"questions":["What pulls Bess''s cart?","Why do the goats love Bess?"],"answers":["Two goats","She feeds them and is kind to them"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-7-4","title":"Lesson XXXIV: The House on Fire","steps":["New words: blaze, put, yet, house, fire, roof, call, ring, we; sound focus: z","You read a line, then your child reads it back; finish by reading the whole lesson together","Slate work: copy “Run, boys, and ring the bell.”","Talk about what your family would do in a fire"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXIV","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00319"}],"questions":["What part of the house is in a blaze?","What are the boys told to do?"],"answers":["The roof","Ring the bell and call men to put out the fire"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-7-5","title":"Lesson XXXV: Review: Tom and Bess","steps":["Let your child read the lesson aloud slowly; help only on words they can''t sound out","Slate work: copy “We can ride to the mill.”","Read it as a play: you are Tom, your child is Bess"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXV","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00327"}],"questions":["How are the logs cut at the mill?","How will Tom and Bess get to the mill?"],"answers":["With a saw","Ride in the goat cart"],"notes":"Review lesson: no new words. Let your child read it as independently as possible and note any words to revisit. Written as a conversation; it reads well with two voices."}]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-u8","title":"Unit 8: Lessons XXXVI–XL","lessons":[{"id":"mcguffey-primer-8-1","title":"Lesson XXXVI: Miss May''s Rule","steps":["New words: Miss, wants, would, tells, rule, keep, good, that, each; sound focus: long u (rule)","Read it once aloud for your child, then have them read it to you (or to a sibling or stuffed animal)","Slate work: copy “This is a good rule.”","Say the rule in your own words and give one example of keeping it"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXVI","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00336"}],"questions":["Why do the children love Miss May?","What is the rule?"],"answers":["She is so kind to them","Do to each one as you would like each one to do to you"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-8-2","title":"Lesson XXXVII: The Schoolhouse","steps":["New words: school, child, church, when, books, slates; sound focus: ch; oo (school)","Read the lesson aloud together, pointing to each word; then let your child read it alone","Slate work: copy “A good child likes to go to school.”","Look at the picture: what makes it look like a church?"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXVII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00342"}],"questions":["Is the building a church or a schoolhouse?","When will the children go in?"],"answers":["A schoolhouse","When the bell rings"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-8-3","title":"Lesson XXXVIII: The Quail","steps":["New words: quail, quick, seen, kill, me, oh, eat, first, know, Henry; sound focus: qu","You read a line, then your child reads it back; finish by reading the whole lesson together","Slate work: copy “It is a quail.”","Read it with two voices, Henry and John"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXVIII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00351"}],"questions":["What bird did Henry find?","Would John like to kill it?"],"answers":["A quail","No"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-8-4","title":"Lesson XXXIX: Baby Kate","steps":["New words: Kate, dear, name, blue, baby, near, shut, crib, sit; sound focus: long a (Kate, baby)","Let your child read the lesson aloud slowly; help only on words they can''t sound out","Slate work: copy “Her name is Kate.”",