stions":["What did the tall tree grow from?","What was made to shine at night?"],"answers":["A small nut","The moon"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-10-7","title":"Lesson LII: The Lord Is Near","steps":["New words: Lord, smile, joys, tears, nigh, morn, griefs, woes, stars, say; sound focus: igh (nigh); oy (joys)","Read it once aloud for your child, then have them read it to you (or to a sibling or stuffed animal)","Slate work: copy “Think the Lord is near.”","Read the hymn slowly; explain nigh, morn, and woes"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson LII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00444"}],"questions":["When does the poem say the stars watch you?","What does the Lord see and hear?"],"answers":["At set of sun","All you do and all you say"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-10-8","title":"Slate Exercises and Script Alphabet","steps":["Sound focus: spelling three-letter words letter by letter","Point to each letter of the slate words (nun, urn, sun, cow...) and blend them into the word","Slate work: copy “c a t  cat”","Trace the script alphabet and numbers 1 to 0 from the last page"],"links":[{"label":"Slate exercises","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00450"},{"label":"Script alphabet","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00455"}],"questions":["What word do the letters s-u-n spell?","What word do the letters h-e-n spell?"],"answers":["sun","hen"],"notes":"This is the Primer''s closing slate and script page, not a story. Spread it over a few days if your child is still learning to write."}]}],"version":1,"license":{"kind":"public_domain"},"attribution":"“McGuffey''s Eclectic Primer, Revised Edition” by William Holmes McGuffey (1881), in the public domain. Free full text: https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/14642. Lesson plan by Freerange."}'::jsonb)
